00:15:52.818 --> 00:15:55.387
.

00:15:55.387 --> 00:15:56.956
Today's wind is

00:15:56.956 --> 00:15:58.190
14 knots

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.692
, blowing from the southwest. Now, I have a question:

00:15:59.692 --> 00:16:01.260
according to our ignorance,

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.294
what

00:16:02.294 --> 00:16:03.696
are

00:16:03.696 --> 00:16:04.797
the conditions today

00:16:04.797 --> 00:16:05.731
? A 14-knot wind should be ideal

00:16:05.731 --> 00:16:06.999
for

00:16:06.999 --> 00:16:09.635
boating. If we were sailing, the wind

00:16:09.635 --> 00:16:11.303
would be excellent.

00:16:11.303 --> 00:16:13.472
When sailing, after pulling up, the tilt

00:16:13.472 --> 00:16:14.907
should be

00:16:14.907 --> 00:16:15.274
around

00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:18.077
15 or 16 degrees,

00:16:18.077 --> 00:16:20.679
and the boat would go very fast. But today, we shouldn't do that. Everyone, if you're going out to feed the fish, that's right.

00:16:20.679 --> 00:16:21.480
Once you go out, it's like

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.949
a (Manchu Han Feast). Basically, before going out, you need to pay attention to these things. Of course, if you're on

00:16:23.949 --> 00:16:26.452
a boat, any boat will be fine. Before going out, you must first check if your

00:16:26.452 --> 00:16:27.586
engine is working properly

00:16:27.586 --> 00:16:29.154
and if you have enough fuel.

00:16:29.154 --> 00:16:31.824
After starting the engine and turning the rudder, check if it's working properly.

00:16:31.824 --> 00:16:32.958
When we get to the side of the boat

00:16:32.958 --> 00:16:34.426
, we usually check the waterline first.

00:16:34.426 --> 00:16:36.595
The waterline doesn't necessarily indicate the exact location,

00:16:36.595 --> 00:16:39.398
but if the position is different from last time,

00:16:39.398 --> 00:16:40.632
be careful;

00:16:40.632 --> 00:16:41.667
it means water might be taking in

00:16:41.667 --> 00:16:42.968
and the boat might be sinking . If

00:16:42.968 --> 00:16:44.470
there's a hole in the boat that you don't know about

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.905
, or a leak that you don't know about,

00:16:46.905 --> 00:16:48.307
water will enter.

00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:50.442
Theoretically, modern boats aren't afraid of this;

00:16:50.442 --> 00:16:52.478
they have automatic drainage systems

00:16:52.478 --> 00:16:54.680
that automatically

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:55.781
discharge wastewater and sewage.

00:16:55.781 --> 00:16:57.116
That is, as long as water

00:16:57.116 --> 00:16:59.151
